    "turn_text": "Sure. I mean, you know, I certainly grew up in the Christian church and learned a lot of great lessons in my youth, although I think I really developed a personal relationship through campus, a crusade for Christ. That's why I'm always, I try to be so supportive of campus based ministries because I think it's a really important time. I mean, people are, that's a time when a lot of people have an opportunity to turn the page from, you know, culturally being Christians to really develop this meaningful salvation. I mean, to really find the grace of the Lord. And at least that was the experience for me. And so I do try to invest in those campus-based ministries. And obviously it's life-changing and not just life, but you know, eternity is a long time. So if you can get an opportunity to grab somebody and show them the way, that's a pretty powerful step you can help them take in their lives.",
