    "turn_text": "think there are blessings that have been bestowed upon this country, that have not been bestowed upon other countries. And I think we don't want to be wanton or careless with that gift either. I mean, Americans have an opportunity to make a greater positive impact on this world than any other peoples. And it's not even really arguable. I mean, I think you'd be hard pressed to find a leader in the international world who would take the counter argument, even just as a thought exercise. And I think also, inarguably, there's been no nation. you know, at least in the last thousand years that comes to mind that is done as much to protect religious liberty or to bring people to Christ and not just Americans, but across the globe. I mean, nobody's done more to protect religious liberty in Africa or in Asia or in South America than Americans have. And again, I think that's incredibly powerful. But I do think we want to keep a certain humility. And again, having that servant leadership approach as opposed to you know, thinking that we're in charge of all things because clearly we're not. I mean, we know who was in charge of all things and that Jesus is not an American, right? I mean, he is greater than citizenship.",
