    "turn_text": "Well, you know, I'm a little torn here because, you know, I'm a flood human being like all of us, right? So I have made plenty of mistakes. And yet I can't help. but feel that things have worked out for me way better than I deserve. I mean, I just haven't made a lot of big mistakes. And lots of little mistakes. I mean, countless, probably billions of little mistakes. And so I don't have a lot of regret. Certainly I have said some words that have hurt people. I've taken some actions that have hurt people. And I would want to try to undo that pain that I've caused to the greatest extent possible. But I think by and large, the advice I would give a young dusty would be to just, you know, do what you're probably going to do anyway, young dusty, which is trust people, maybe a little too much. Maybe a lot of people are a little too much. I'm a sometime accused of people, even that I work with of being not naive. They won't use that word, but of expecting the best in people. And I know politics is a cynical business, but I have been, I have been pleasantly surprised by way more people in this planet than I have been disappointed. And that's even coming from somebody who maybe trusts too much and hopes too much. and loves to watch. And so maybe that is naive. But I would tell you, people are great. And I just think life is a lot better when you take an opportunity to be optimistic and to be caring.",
